    "title": "In 2014, Akon co-founded Akon Lighting Africa to bring solar power to rural Africa; within a year, it was reaching communities across 14 countries | World News",
    "text": "Why this project was important\nThe need was huge. Tracking SDG 7: The Energy Progress Report 2026, a joint report by the IEA, IRENA, the UN, the World Bank, and the WHO, shows that 655 million people in the world still live without electricity, with more than 560 million of them in Sub-Saharan Africa. In 2024, 92 percent of people had access globally. That sounds high, but progress has run out of steam, leaving sub-Saharan Africa and rural areas behind. The report also finds the number of rural people without power in that region increased from 376 million in 2010 to 447 million in 2024. For many readers, steady power is simply part of daily life. The numbers show how uneven access remains around the world.",
